Package: silvdelta
Title: Structural Change Detection in Forests from Bi-Temporal Point Clouds
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R:
    person("Mateus", "dos Santos Neves", email = "nevesms@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A methodological pipeline to detect and quantify structural
    changes in forest stands from two point clouds of the same area acquired
    before (t0) and after (t1) a management intervention such as pruning or
    thinning. Provides co-registration of epochs on stable structures, a
    common terrain model, stem detection with or without user seeds,
    voxel-based change detection with a registration-aware tolerance,
    individual-tree and area-based change metrics, rule-based classification
    of the intervention and calibration of removed biomass against field data.
    Works with terrestrial, mobile (SLAM) and UAV laser scanning clouds.
